<figure class="cache-figure" data-production-contract>
 <p class="figure-title">One product, two promises</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><button data-prev>Previous contract step</button><button data-next>Next contract step</button><button data-reset>Reset contract</button></div>
 <p class="cluster-stage" data-stage></p>
 <div class="recovery-pair"><div class="recovery-node"><b>Authoritative source</b><strong data-source></strong><span data-source-status></span></div><div class="recovery-node"><b>Redis display copy</b><strong data-cache></strong><span>Original deadline: 2,000 ms</span></div></div>
 <div class="restore-timelines"><span>Age of the original observation · <b data-age></b></span><div class="restore-track"><i style="width:80%"></i><b data-clock></b></div><div class="restore-axis"><span>0 ms</span><span>Deadline 2,000 · axis 2,500 ms</span></div></div>
 <div class="contract-answers"><div><b>Display read</b><strong data-display></strong><span>Accept an observation younger than 2 seconds</span></div><div><b>Authoritative price check</b><strong data-authoritative></strong><span>Read the source for this operation</span></div></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>A fixed schedule, not live execution. The old read was already in flight when the write committed. In the last step an old Redis entry is deliberately still present, as it could be after a delayed fill or restore; the application checks its payload deadline anyway. The two read outcomes represent separate operations. Prices are in pence; time is in milliseconds.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{contractSteps,contractOutcome}from'../../lib/caching/system-design.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-production-contract]').forEach(root=>{let step=0;const prev=root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-prev]')!,next=root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-next]')!;const render=()=>{const s=contractSteps[step],out=contractOutcome(s);for(const[k,v]of Object.entries({stage:`${step+1} / ${contractSteps.length} · ${s.title}`,source:`${s.source} pence`,'source-status':s.available?'Available':'Unavailable',cache:s.cache===null?'Empty':`${s.cache} pence`,age:`${s.time} ms`,display:out.display,authoritative:out.authoritative,explanation:s.note}))root.querySelector(`[data-${k}]`)!.textContent=v;root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-clock]')!.style.left=`${s.time/2500*100}%`;prev.disabled=step===0;next.disabled=step===contractSteps.length-1;};prev.onclick=()=>{step--;render();};next.onclick=()=>{step++;render();};root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.onclick=()=>{step=0;render();};render();});
</script>
